        "path": "cuprum/pump_events.py",
        "line": 168,
        "display": "PumpHook = cabc.Callable[[PumpEvent], None]",
        "doc": {
          "summary": "A synchronous consumer of <a href=\"#PumpEvent\"><code>PumpEvent</code></a> values.",
          "body": [
            "Pump hooks are synchronous by contract. Every emission site is synchronous — one on the Python-pump fall-back path and the others inside cancellation unwinding — so there is no task to attach an awaitable to and no point at which awaiting it could be ordered against the transfer it describes. A hook that returns an awaitable is reported and discarded rather than run."
          ]
        }
