        "display": "from cuprum.adapters import echo_metrics",
        "doc": {
          "summary": "Metrics adapter for stream-echo failure and truncation events.",
          "body": [
            "Counts how often a text-only echo sink rejected the subprocess output, per output stream, and how often a bounded echoed line was successfully truncated. Those facts are otherwise visible only through a <code>WARNING</code> log record or the echo observation hook, which dashboards cannot aggregate.",
            "The hook consumes <a href=\"#EchoEvent\"><code>EchoEvent</code></a> values from <a href=\"#observe_echo\"><code>observe_echo</code></a>. It reuses the <code>MetricsCollector</code> protocol, so one collector can back the execution, pump, and echo hooks and no new telemetry dependency is introduced."
          ],
          "examples": "::\n\n    from cuprum import sh\n    from cuprum.adapters.echo_metrics import EchoMetricsHook\n    from cuprum.adapters.metrics_adapter import InMemoryMetrics\n    from cuprum.echo_observation import observe_echo\n\n    metrics = InMemoryMetrics()\n\n    with sh.observe(MetricsHook(metrics)), observe_echo(EchoMetricsHook(metrics)):\n        command.run_sync(output=RunOutputOptions(echo=True))\n\n    print(metrics.counters[\"cuprum_echo_encoding_failures_total\"])"
        },
        "members": [
          {
            "name": "ECHO_ENCODING_FAILURES_TOTAL",
            "kind": "constant",
            "display": "ECHO_ENCODING_FAILURES_TOTAL = 'cuprum_echo_encoding_failures_total'",
            "doc": {
              "summary": "Echo writes rejected with <code>UnicodeEncodeError</code>, labelled by <code>stream</code>.",
              "body": [
                "The only other label is <code>error_category</code>, whose single value (<code>UNICODE_ENCODE</code>) names the closed category the counter counts. The label exists so a future failure category extends the metric rather than silently mixing into this series."
              ]
            }
